                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names (name of St Mary in <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>);
                           supplication formulas with the name of the original donor/owner; titles
                           and numbers of the Psalms, Canticles and Songs; title of <ref target="#ms_i1.1"/>, <ref target="#ms_i1.2"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>; 
                           title and incipit of the daily readings of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>; name of the
                           Hebrew letters in <ref cRef="betmas:LIT2000Mazmur.Ps118">Psalm 118</ref>; refrains of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/> (written out
                           fully or abbreviated); elements of the punctuation marks and text dividers; Ethiopic numerals or their elements. 
                           A few lines (alternating with black lines) on the opening page of text <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>; a few lines (alternating with black lines) of the incipit of <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>.</seg>
                     </handNote>
