                  <additions>
                     <list>
                        <item xml:id="a1">
                           <locus target="#164r"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3622Miracle">Miracle of Mary: Homily on a potter from Syria</title>. The name of the supplicant has been erased; the miracle is written by a mediocre hand, the incipit is written twice.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ስምዑ፡ አበውየ፡ ወአኀውየ፡ ከመ፡ ንንግርክሙ፡ ዘንተ፡ ተአምረ፡ ዓባየ፡ ዘገብረት፡ እግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ማርያም፡ ድንግል፡ በ፪ጥዕምተ፡ ስም፡ ሕይወተ፡ ዓለም፡ ዘነገሩነ፡ አበው፡ ቅዱሳን፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/>
                              ነበረ፡ በምድረ፡ ሶርያ፡ ፩ ብእሲ፡ ለበሐዊ<sic/>፡ ፈራሄ፡ እግዚአብሔር።</q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a2">
                           <locus from="180ra" to="185ra"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2835RepCh119">Malkǝʾa Mikāʾel</title>; the name of the supplicant has been erased from the final line. It is written by a fine hand. 
                              The divine names and the word <foreign>‘salām’</foreign> (also abbreviated) are rubricated.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ሰላም፡ ለዝክረ፡ <add place="above">ስምከ፡ ምስለ፡</add> ስመ፡ ልዑል፡ ዘተሳተፈ። ወልደ፡ ያሬድ፡ ሄኖክ፡ በከመ፡ ጸሐፈ። ሶበ፡ እጼውዕ፡ ስመከ፡ ከሢትየ፡ አፈ። ረዳኤ፡ ምንዱባን፡ 
                              <hi rend="rubric">ሚካኤል፡</hi> በከመ፡ ታለምድ፡ ዘልፈ።</q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a3">
                           <locus target="#185v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">Protective prayer (?). It is written in a careless way.</desc>            
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e1">
                           <locus target="#5r #5v #16v #17r #20r #22v #30r #32v"/>
                           <desc type="Directive">Directives for praying with the Psalms are written in the upper margin, in a secondary hand.</desc> 
                        </item>
                           <item xml:id="e2">
                              <locus target="#113v #119r"/>
                           <desc>The scribe reduced the size of his handwriting.</desc>
